    "result_text": "The full test suite consists of the single `AcceptanceTest` class (plus the `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` support classes), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented idempotent owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the handler for `POST /api/owners`):\n\n- **Reads the `Idempotency-Key` header** via `RequestContextHolder`, since the OpenAPI-generated `OwnersApi.addOwner` signature has no header parameter (`currentIdempotencyKey()` returns `null` when the header is absent/blank).\n- **On a repeat** with an already-seen key, it looks up the originally created owner and returns it with **200 OK** \u2014 skipping all validation and the duplicate check that would otherwise 409.\n- **On a fresh create**, after the owner is saved it records `key \u2192 owner.id` in a `ConcurrentHashMap`, then returns the normal **201 Created**.\n\nThe `coreIdempotentRepeat` test confirms the first create returns 2xx and the second (same key, same payload) returns 200 with the identical owner id instead of a 409 duplicate. `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
