    "probe_text": "Confirmed: `POST /api/owners` maps to `addOwner(...)` in `OwnerRestControllerV1` (openapi.yml line 65\u201369). Here is everything that happens, in execution order.\n\n## Guard (before the method body)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN)\")`; caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:520`).\n- **Bean validation of the body** \u2014 the generated `OwnersApi` applies `@Valid` to the `OwnerFieldsDto`, so any DTO-level constraints are enforced before the code below runs.\n\n## `addOwner` body, in order\n\n**1. Idempotency short-circuit** (`:526`) \u2014 reads the `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key was already seen *and* the owner it created still exists, the method returns that original owner with **200 OK** and does nothing else (no new record).\n\n**2. Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`:536`) \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner`, with `id` and `pets` ignored.\n\n**3. Postcode validation** (`isPostcodeValid`, `:537`) \u2192 **400** if invalid. Absent postcode is OK; if present it must be exactly 4 digits, and if the owner's *city* maps to a known region (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD) the postcode must fall in that region's range (2000\u20132099 / 3000\u20133099 / 4000\u20134099).\n\n**4. Telephone validation** (`:540`) \u2192 **400** if `toE164` returns null or `hasValidNationalLength` fails. Normalizes to E.164 (strips separators, defaults country code to `+61`, drops a leading `0`), requires 8\u201315 digits, and enforces national length for `+61` (9 digits) / `+1` (10 digits). *(Result held aside; stored in step 8.)*\n\n**5. Email normalization + validation** (`normalizeEmail`, `:544`) \u2192 **400** if present-but-invalid. **Side effects:** absent/empty email \u2192 set to `null`; otherwise must match the email regex and its domain must not be on the disposable-domain blocklist (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail), then the email is **lower-cased and set** on the owner.\n\n**6. Address composition** (`composeAddress`, `:547`) \u2192 **400** if it yields nothing. **Side effects:** prefers structured `addressLine1`(+`addressLine2`), normalizing them **in place** (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET/RD\u2192ROAD/AVE\u2192AVENUE); otherwise normalizes the flat `address`.\n\n**7. `setAddress(...)`** (`:551`) \u2014 store the composed address (side effect).\n\n**8. `setTelephone(...)`** (`:552`) \u2014 store the E.164 telephone from step 4 (side effect).\n\n**9. Future-date validation** (`:553`) \u2192 **400** if a supplied `registrationDate` is after today.\n\n**10. Compute business-day registration date** (`toBusinessDay`, `:557`) \u2014 supplied date or today, rolled forward past weekends and listed 2026 public holidays. *(Stored in step 21.)*\n\n**11. Daily-limit validation** (`:559`) \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests** if `DAILY_CREATE_LIMIT` (100) owners already have that registration date.\n\n**12. City-capacity validation** (`:563`) \u2192 **409 Conflict** if the owner's city already holds `CITY_CAPACITY` (50) owners.\n\n**13. `setHouseholdId(...)`** (`:569`) \u2014 deterministic SHA-256 over normalized lastName + `|` + postcode (side effect).\n\n**14. Hard-duplicate validation** (`:576`) \u2192 **409 Conflict** if the owner's full `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) equals any non-deleted existing owner's.\n\n**15. Household-duplicate validation** (`:588`) \u2192 **409 Conflict** if another owner shares this (lastName, postcode) household *and* the request did **not** set `sharesHousehold`.\n\n**16. `setPossibleDuplicate` / `setPossibleDuplicateOf`** (`:593`) \u2014 if the caller declared a household member, both are cleared (false/null); otherwise flagged when an existing owner shares lastName+postcode but has a different telephone (smallest id wins). Side effect.\n\n**17. `setNamesakeCount(...)`** (`:602`) \u2014 count of existing owners with the same first+last name (side effect).\n\n**18. `setHouseholdSize(...)`** (`:603`) \u2014 household members + 1 (side effect).\n\n**19. `setBulkSignupWarning(...)`** (`:604`) \u2014 true if more than `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD` (80) owners already registered that day (side effect).\n\n**20. `setRegistrationDate(...)`** (`:605`) \u2014 the business-day-adjusted date from step 10 (side effect).\n\n**21. `setCustomerCode(...)`** (`customerCodeFor`, `:606`) \u2014 `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode; SHA-256 hash of telephone+lastName), with `-<n>` appended on collision to stay unique (side effect).\n\n**22. Persist** (`clinicService.saveOwner`, `:607`) \u2014 the owner is saved to the database (primary side effect; assigns the id).\n\n**23. Record idempotency key** (`:608`) \u2014 if a key was present, store `key \u2192 new owner id` in the in-memory `idempotentCreates` map (side effect).\n\n**24. Audit log** (`:611`) \u2014 `AUDIT.info(...)` writes an audit-trail line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, and derived membershipLevel/membershipNumber (side effect).\n\n**25. Respond** (`:614`) \u2014 map to `OwnerDto`, set the `Location` header to `/api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n**Note on the response DTO:** `toOwnerDto` derives many additional fields at mapping time (`displayName`, `initials`, `salutation`, `membershipNumber`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipPoints`, `fiscalYear`, `checkDigit`, `locality`, `timezone`, `contactPreference`, `ageBand`, `telephoneDisplay`, `selfLink`). These are computed for the response only \u2014 they are **not** persisted validations or stored side-effects."
